 | `paths.js` | 222 | Resolves `TASKFERRY_STATE_DIR`/`TASKFERRY_RUNTIME_DIR`/`TASKFERRY_CACHE_DIR` and the socket path from XDG defaults + env overrides. Exports `TASKFERRY_PLUMBING_ENV_VARS` (frozen array of those five names, now including `TASKFERRY_OVERLAY_TMP_DIR`) so `tasks.js` builds its caller-env exclusion set from the same source of truth — a new plumbing var added here lands in the exclusion set automatically. `resolveOverlayTmpRoot()` scopes the CoW overlay root under `resolveRuntimeDir()` (not plain `os.tmpdir()`) so two daemon instances — isolated via `TASKFERRY_STATE_DIR`/`RUNTIME_DIR` or not — never share an overlay namespace; a restarting/crash-looping daemon's startup orphan sweep used to be able to delete a *different* daemon's in-flight overlay because every daemon on the host shared plain `/tmp` regardless of state/runtime isolation (taskferry#286). `TASKFERRY_OVERLAY_TMP_DIR` is an explicit escape hatch to pin the overlay root elsewhere. Also `resolveWorkspaceRoot()`: the git workspace root (handles plain repo/worktree/submodule/bare-repo layouts) that `list`/`watch`/`context`/`home` default `--directory` to — `dispatch`/`advisor` deliberately keep their default on literal cwd instead, since that value doubles as the sandbox root. `createWorkspaceRootResolver()` memoizes `resolveWorkspaceRoot()` per directory (one instance created per `startDaemon()` call in `daemon.js`, so its cache is scoped to that daemon's lifetime, not a module-level global) so repeated directory comparisons don't re-spawn `git` each time; `sameWorkspace(a, b, resolveRoot)` is the shared comparison both `daemon.js`'s `filteredTaskDetails()`/`filteredList()` and `daemon-server.js`'s `deliverEvent()` use instead of a raw `===`, so a repo-root-scoped `list`/`context`/`watch` also matches a task dispatched into one of that repo's linked worktrees (taskferry#315) — the literal-equality fast path inside it skips calling `resolveRoot` (and, on a cache miss, spawning git) for the common same-directory case. |
 | `narration-format.js` | 24 | Formats a task's narration/activity text for display. |
